{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/mcr/hello-world","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:14.747Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/mcr/hello-world/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/mcr/hello-world/about"},"readme":"## About\nThis artifact is an example docker container. This artifact is maintained by the MCR Team.\nCheck in for updates.\n\n## Featured tags\n    docker pull mcr.microsoft.com/mcr/hello-world:v1.0\n    \n|Tags  | Architecture | OS |\n|------|--------------|----|\n| v1.0 | AMD64 | Linux|\n| v2.0 | ARM64 | Linux\n\n\n## Configuration\nYou must also have Docker installed locally. Docker provides packages that easily configure Docker on any [Mac](#), [Windows](#), or [Linux](#) system.\n\n## Usage\n### Container sample: Run a simple application\nType the following command to run a sample console application:\n    docker run --rm mcr.microsoft.com/mcr/hello-world\n### Container sample: Run a web application\nType the following command to run a sample console application:\n    docker run -it --rm -p 8000:80 --name hello-world mcr.microsoft.com/mcr/hello-world\nAfter the application starts, navigate to http://localhost:8000 in your web browser.\nSee Hosting [Hello World](#) with Docker over HTTPS to use HTTPS with this image.\n\n## Support\n[File an issue](#)\n[Contact Microsoft Support](#)\n[Hello World Support Lifecycle](#)\n\n## License\nMicrosoft containers are licensed under various licenses depending upon the container’s content. If the container has a Debian, Ubuntu or Alpine Linux base image and you want to retrieve the licenses, copyright notices or source code information for the base image and its official packages, please review the Linux Legal Metadata instructions file. If you are using a Windows based container the governing licenses are referenced in this Docker Hub “License” section or in the container itself, usually as a NOTICE or LICENSE file. All other components (whether open or closed source) are licensed as indicated either in this Docker Hub “License” section or in the container itself.\nThis container may incorporate material from third parties. Microsoft makes certain open source code available at https://3rdpartysource.microsoft.com, or if you want a copy of the source code in this container you may send a check or money order for US $5.00, including the product name, the open source component name, and version number, to: Source Code Compliance Team, Microsoft Corporation, One Microsoft Way, Redmond, WA 98052 USA\nFor more information visit the [MCR GitHub for Licensing](https://github.com/microsoft/containerregistry/blob/main/legal/Container-Images-Legal-Notice.md).","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2024-10-12T00:55:49.4779207+00:00","categories":["Monitoring"],"keywords":[],"license":"MIT","links":[],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"222.1M+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"Canary-IngestionTest223","digest":"sha256:d0e7fa7045dd684a72dabcd9c5e6bf78d6727205832cb03c3d797e7a3f5d81ba","pushed":"2023-05-20T06:23:19.0000000+00:00","size":1667,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"Wus2-IngestionTest2","digest":"sha256:d0e7fa7045dd684a72dabcd9c5e6bf78d6727205832cb03c3d797e7a3f5d81ba","pushed":"2023-05-19T05:42:13.0000000+00:00","size":1667,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"Canary-IngestionTest222","digest":"sha256:d0e7fa7045dd684a72dabcd9c5e6bf78d6727205832cb03c3d797e7a3f5d81ba","pushed":"2023-01-10T18:14:49.0000000+00:00","size":1667,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"Canary-IngestionTestTMTest4","dig